// MUST FAIL: `*T` as a pointer type. DESIGN.md:340 — "(`*` is reserved for exports,
// so raw pointers are `Ptr<T>`)". This is the one place DESIGN.md states a
// prohibition to protect a token: `*` after a name means exported, so it can never
// also mean "pointer to".

str* = {
    data: *u8,
    len: usize,
}
